ween the small coves of Rathmoylan and Ballymacaw.","wpu":"The White Lady (Ireland)","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/WhiteLadyDunmoreCloseup.jpg/960px-WhiteLadyDunmoreCloseup.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Harristown Passage Tomb","g":"sights","k":"archaeological_site","la":52.184166,"lo":-7.012228,"d":4041},{"n":"Ballymacaw Cove","g":"sights","k":"beach","la":52.139631,"lo":-7.056155,"d":4527},{"n":"St. Dubhan's Church","g":"sights","k":"attraction","la":52.134239,"lo":-6.927221,"d":4755},{"n":"hook","g":"sights","k":"attraction","la":52.129655,"lo":-6.929821,"d":4808},{"n":"Lime Kiln","g":"sights","k":"ruins","la":52.141315,"lo":-6.922321,"d":4851},{"n":"Lime Kiln","g":"sights","k":"ruins","la":52.127164,"lo":-6.929479,"d":4965},{"n":"Hook Lighthouse Visitors Center","g":"sights","k":"attraction","la":52.124065,"lo":-6.928977,"d":5178,"h":"Jul-Aug: Mo-Su,PH 09:30-19:00; Sep-Jun: Mo-Su,PH 09:30-17:00","w":"https://www.hookheritage.ie","ph":"+353 51 397 055"},{"n":"Woodstown Strand","g":"sights","k":"beach","la":52.197125,"lo":-6.976572,"d":5344},{"n":"The Hall Bay","g":"sights","k":"beach","la":52.147022,"lo":-6.91331,"d":5379},{"n":"Slade Castle","g":"sights","k":"castle","la":52.133835,"lo":-6.910635,"d":5836,"wp":"en:Slade Castle","ds":"Slade Castle is a tower house and National Monument in County Wexford, Ireland. It is located in the village of Slade on the Hook Peninsula and primarily dates to the late 15th or early 16th century.","wpu":"Slade Castle","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Slade_Castle.jpg/960px-Slade_Castle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Boyce's Bay","g":"sights","k":"beach","la":52.156264,"lo":-6.900575,"d":6276},{"n":"Dromina Strand","g":"sights","k":"beach","la":52.206045,"lo":-6.973323,"d":6360},{"n":"Otter Hole","g":"sights","k":"beach","la":52.169578,"lo":-6.90015,"d":6632},{"n":"Windmill","g":"sights","k":"ruins","la":52.159195,"lo":-6.891383,"d":6939},{"n":"Templetown Bay Beach","g":"sights","k":"beach","la":52.178616,"lo":-6.901412,"d":6949},{"n":"Brecaun Church","g":"sights","k":"ruins","la":52.151434,"lo":-6.889461,"d":6997},{"n":"Raheen Strand","g":"sights","k":"beach","la":52.213679,"lo":-6.976552,"d":7158},{"n":"Sandeel Bay","g":"sights","k":"beach","la":52.161177,"lo":-6.881902,"d":7613},{"n":"Bank of Ireland","g":"essentials","k":"atm","la":52.148227,"lo":-6.993944,"d":237},{"n":"Euronet","g":"essentials","k":"atm","la":52.147704,"lo":-6.993058,"d":265},{"n":"Dunmore East Post Office","g":"essentials","k":"post_office","la":52.147659,"lo":-6.993076,"d":270,"w":"https://www.anpost.com/"},{"n":"Mulligans Pharmacy","g":"essentials","k":"pharmacy","la":52.147506,"lo":-6.992911,"d":284},{"n":"Dunmore East","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":52.155,"lo":-6.996,"d":619,"ds":"Dunmore East (Irish: Dún Mór Thóir, meaning 'east big fort') is a tourist and fishing town in County Waterford, Ireland. Situated on the west side of Waterford Harbour on Ireland's southeastern coast, it lies within the barony of Gaultier (An Gháilltír – \"land of the foreigner\" in Irish); a reference to the influx of Viking and Norman settlers in the area.","wpu":"Dunmore East","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/e5/Irl_DunmoreEast_harbour.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},{"n":"Waterford Harbour","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":52.183333,"lo":-6.933333,"d":5454,"ds":"Waterford Harbour (Irish: Loch Dá Chaoch / Cuan Phort Láirge) is a natural harbour at the mouth of the Three Sisters; the River Nore, the River Suir and the River Barrow in Ireland. It is navigable for shipping to both Waterford and New Ross. The Port of Waterford is capable of accommodating vessels up to 32,000 tons dwt.","wpu":"Waterford Harbour","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/df/Angry_Sky_-_geograph.org.uk_-_834308.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},{"n":"Duncannon","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":52.221,"lo":-6.932,"d":8891,"ds":"Duncannon (Irish: Dún Canann) is a village in southwest County Wexford, Ireland. Bordered to the west by Waterford harbour and sitting on a rocky headland jutting into the channel is the strategically prominent Duncannon Fort which dominates the village. Primarily a fishing village, Duncannon also relies on tourism and is situated on the marked \"Ring of Hook\" drive.","wpu":"Duncannon","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/4f/Duncannon_Fort_-_geograph.org.uk_-_546482.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},{"n":"Ballygunner Castle","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":52.228,"lo":-7.0565,"d":9724,"ds":"Ballygunner Castle is a country house in the Ballygunner area of County Waterford in Ireland. It is believed to be built on the site of a former Viking stronghold. The main structure of the house includes a combination of medieval and 17th century building, with evidence of further modifications in the 18th and 19th centuries.","wpu":"Ballygunner Castle","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/Castles_of_Munster-_Ballygunner%2C_Waterford_%283%29_%28geograph_4570343%29.jpg/960px-Castles_of_Munster-_Ballygunner%2C_Waterford_%283%29_%28geograph_4570343%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Passage East","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":52.2391,"lo":-6.97274,"d":9994,"ds":"Passage East (Irish: An Pasáiste, meaning 'the passage') is a fishing village in County Waterford, Ireland, situated on the west bank of Waterford Harbour. It is 12 km from Waterford city 10 km from Dunmore East and 21 km from Tramore.","wpu":"Passage East","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/a4/The_first_ferry_of_the_day_from_Passage_East_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1388506.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"}],"about":{"ds":"Waterford (Irish: Port Láirge [pˠɔɾˠt̪ˠ ˈl̪ˠaːɾʲ(ə)ɟə]) is a city in County Waterford in the south-east of Ireland. It is located within the province of Munster. The city is situated at the head of Waterford Harbour.","wpu":"Waterford","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/cf/Reginalds_Tower_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},"wk":"2026-10-18"}